{% if availableSteps %}
<available_observation_tasks>
Follow-up image tasks you may add to `pending_steps` if high-res processing is warranted:
{% for step in availableSteps %}- {{ step }}
{% endfor %}</available_observation_tasks>
{% endif %}

{% if availableAnalysis %}
<available_analysis_tasks>
Analysis tasks you may add to `analysis_tasks` based on content type:
{% for step in availableAnalysis %}- {{ step }}
{% endfor %}</available_analysis_tasks>
{% endif %}

{% if operatorHint %}
<operator_hint>
{% for k, v in operatorHint %}{{ k }}: {{ v }}
{% endfor %}
</operator_hint>
{% endif %}

{% if existingMetadata %}
<existing_metadata>
{% for k, v in existingMetadata %}{{ k }}: {{ v }}
{% endfor %}
</existing_metadata>
{% endif %}

{% if existingMetadata.location is defined and existingMetadata.location %}
<objective_grounding>
The location and date in existing_metadata are sourced catalog facts about when and where the
photograph was taken — NOT file EXIF (a scanned negative's EXIF reflects digitization, not capture).
Use them only to GROUND your reading, never to override what is visually present: transcribe any
text, signs, or place-names visible in the image in the language(s) of {{ existingMetadata.location }}
(e.g. Hungarian for Hungary) — do not default to Cyrillic or another script unless unmistakably present.
</objective_grounding>
{% endif %}

Observe the image and return the JSON envelope described in your instructions.
